{
	"name": "Add Google Sheets contacts to a ThunderPhone campaign and start it after approval",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Add Google Sheets contacts to a ThunderPhone campaign and start it after approval\n\nLoad a Google Sheets call list into an empty draft ThunderPhone campaign and start it after approval.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Get campaign** and **Empty draft?** stop unless the **Settings** campaign is an empty draft, so a re-run stops before adding contacts again.\n2. **Keep rows with consent** keeps sheet rows with a phone number and `yes` in `consent_to_call`.\n3. **Map contact fields** sends only `phone_number`, `lead_id` and `first_name`, once per number.\n4. **Add contacts to draft campaign** uploads the list. **Start campaign** runs only after form approval (24-hour limit).\n\n### Setup\n1. An instance owner or admin installs the verified **ThunderPhone** node (`n8n-nodes-thunderphone`) from the nodes panel.\n2. Add a ThunderPhone server API key (**Organization > Keys**) in n8n as a **ThunderPhone API** credential. Its user must be an admin or owner. Select it in **Get campaign** too.\n3. Create a Draft campaign with an agent and an outbound-enabled From Number, and paste its ID into **Settings**.\n4. Create a `Contacts` tab with `lead_id`, `phone_number` (E.164), `first_name` and `consent_to_call`, then pick it in **Read contact rows**.\n5. Read the confirmation in **Start campaign** and turn it on.\n\n### Customization\n- Add columns in **Map contact fields** for more call variables. Up to 5,000 contacts per run.\n\n### Data handling\nCall transcripts and summaries can contain personal or health information. Add them only if your organization is allowed to store that data in the connected app, and under a BAA where health information is involved. Rows you copy into Google Sheets stay there until you delete them. Set a retention rule that fits your data.",
				"height": 980,
				"width": 640
			},
			"id": "6b38a174-b474-5f33-bea4-458c6aef501e",
			"name": "Template overview",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [-760, -260]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## 1. Check the campaign\nStops unless the campaign is a draft with no contacts.",
				"height": 620,
				"width": 820,
				"color": 7
			},
			"id": "66f5aff2-1997-52b5-b6dc-d7d95c4b0312",
			"name": "Section: check campaign",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [140, -20]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## 2. Load the call list\nReads the sheet, keeps rows with consent and removes duplicate numbers.",
				"height": 380,
				"width": 980,
				"color": 7
			},
			"id": "c9f72df1-b865-51c1-9232-78d444f23303",
			"name": "Section: load contacts",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [1000, -20]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "### Not deduplicated\nThunderPhone keeps every contact you add, so **Empty draft?** only lets this step run on a draft with no contacts.",
				"height": 600,
				"width": 240,
				"color": 3
			},
			"id": "bea70d83-3b93-5476-afa8-8848bfec6183",
			"name": "Warning: add contacts",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [1990, -240]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## 3. Approve, then start\nNothing is called until someone approves in the form.",
				"height": 620,
				"width": 440,
				"color": 7
			},
			"id": "493f6ad2-87aa-5182-b9ab-71c3420112a1",
			"name": "Section: approve and start",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [2260, -20]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "### Real calls\nStarting dials every contact and spends ThunderPhone credits. Turn the confirmation on once you have read it.\n\nIf this step fails after contacts were added, start the campaign in ThunderPhone instead of re-running.\n\nYour organization is responsible for having consent to call each number and for following the calling laws that apply.",
				"height": 600,
				"width": 320,
				"color": 3
			},
			"id": "434b622c-f8ec-5529-bea7-eaa7973e8ffa",
			"name": "Warning: start campaign",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [2720, -300]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {},
			"id": "eee61fb0-4653-555e-9953-ab043a73b73e",
			"name": "Run import",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [0, 180]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"assignments": {
					"assignments": [
						{
							"id": "a22ff994-b19c-534e-aeda-3d190cc2dfbe",
							"name": "campaignId",
							"value": "PASTE_DRAFT_CAMPAIGN_ID",
							"type": "string"
						}
					]
				},
				"options": {}
			},
			"id": "23906b31-e2a0-5713-9806-0332fb9a2e12",
			"name": "Settings",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
			"typeVersion": 3.4,
			"position": [200, 180]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"url": "=https://api.thunderphone.com/v1/campaigns/{{ encodeURIComponent($json.campaignId.trim()) }}",
				"authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
				"nodeCredentialType": "thunderPhoneApi",
				"options": {}
			},
			"id": "e8c1c9a8-65eb-5967-9b95-4691cfed43a1",
			"name": "Get campaign",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
			"typeVersion": 4.2,
			"position": [400, 180]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"conditions": {
					"options": {
						"caseSensitive": true,
						"leftValue": "",
						"typeValidation": "strict",
						"version": 2
					},
					"conditions": [
						{
							"id": "2f72a3cb-29fa-5c24-a680-8881c6844ce2",
							"leftValue": "={{ $json.status }}",
							"rightValue": "draft",
							"operator": {
								"type": "string",
								"operation": "equals"
							}
						},
						{
							"id": "cb49f205-0662-56ef-a0d4-151aae4c4184",
							"leftValue": "={{ Number($json.total_count ?? 0) + ($json.contacts ?? []).length }}",
							"rightValue": 0,
							"operator": {
								"type": "number",
								"operation": "equals"
							}
						}
					],
					"combinator": "and"
				},
				"options": {}
			},
			"id": "5a7ca243-f277-579b-8479-1c876e252e34",
			"name": "Empty draft?",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
			"typeVersion": 2.2,
			"position": [600, 180]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
